\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3.7}{\ignorespaces Extreme world, filtered runs: when the error rises, where, and how long the filter ran. ``Onset'' is the first time the start-anchored position error stays above $3\times $ the estimator's static median for \SI {1}{\second } (threshold in the text); ``where'' gives the route progress at that moment and whether the robot was on a straight or in a heading change (ground-truth yaw rate above \SI {10}{\degree \per \second }). ``Filter until'' is the end of the initial stretch of \SI {5}{\second } windows with a mask on at least \SI {98}{\percent } of frames; ``unmasked'' is the image area left after masking on matched frames, median (minimum). Times are seconds from the ground-truth start.\relax }}{10}{table.caption.21}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:extreme-timelines-filtered}{{3.7}{10}{Extreme world, filtered runs: when the error rises, where, and how long the filter ran. ``Onset'' is the first time the start-anchored position error stays above $3\times $ the estimator's static median for \SI {1}{\second } (threshold in the text); ``where'' gives the route progress at that moment and whether the robot was on a straight or in a heading change (ground-truth yaw rate above \SI {10}{\degree \per \second }). ``Filter until'' is the end of the initial stretch of \SI {5}{\second } windows with a mask on at least \SI {98}{\percent } of frames; ``unmasked'' is the image area left after masking on matched frames, median (minimum). Times are seconds from the ground-truth start.\relax }{table.caption.21}{}}
\newlabel{tab:extreme-timelines-filtered@cref}{{[table][7][4]3.7}{[1][9][]10}}
